Meta/DINOv2 and ByteDance/Depth Anything-derived components retain their
copyright and Apache notices in the source files. The Apache License 2.0 text
is preserved in licenses/Apache-2.0.txt. Copied model definitions are
retained where necessary to load existing checkpoint parameters, including
frozen heads that the training/inference entrypoints do not execute.

The source project's reconstruction lineage includes CroCo; the CroCo and DUSt3R
runtime, visualization code and CUDA extension are not distributed by this
minimal package.
No upstream component, checkpoint or dataset is relicensed by the root CC BY 4.0
license.

DROID and RoboTwin sample exports retain their original source metadata with
machine paths made portable. Upstream model checkpoints and source datasets
remain subject to their upstream terms.

The Python implementation uses the tcp4d package and TCP4D/TCP4DPolicy names.
The offline checkpoint converter updates serialized parameter names on disk;
the runtime accepts the current TCP4D checkpoint schema strictly.

The DROID augmentation workbench adds optional SAM3, cuRobo, SAPIEN and
ProPainter integrations. Those externally installed repositories, downloaded
checkpoints and robot meshes retain their upstream terms. In particular,
ProPainter's code and models retain NTU S-Lab License 1.0 terms. See
aug_pipeline/README.md and aug_pipeline/resources.json for provenance.
